{"test_id": "B24-001", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B24", "input": {"question": "Incident response scenario 1: A CII organization experiences a cyber security incident. What CCoP 2.0 Section 8 actions are required for classification and reporting?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "serious", "expected_response": "CCoP 2.0 does not define a Code-level serious/substantial classification scheme or prescribe Form A1/A2 labels or fixed hour-count reporting deadlines in the Code itself. The grounded response is to activate the Cybersecurity Incident Response Plan, follow the incident-reporting structure in the plan so the CIIO complies with the Cybersecurity Act and other applicable laws, contain the affected systems or access path as appropriate, and preserve digital forensic evidence. The CIIO should isolate the affected systems, assess the impact on essential services, and trigger backup, restoration, business continuity or disaster recovery procedures where service delivery is affected. Reference: CCoP 2.0 §7.1.1(b), §7.1.1(g), §7.1.1(h), §8.2.1.", "key_facts": [{"fact": "Serious incident = 2-hour CSA reporting (Form A2)", "source": "CCoP 2.0 Section 8.3", "tier": "critical"}, {"fact": "Substantial incident = 24-hour CSA reporting (Form A1)", "source": "CCoP 2.0 Section 8.3", "tier": "important"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Delayed reporting is acceptable", "Minor incidents don't need reporting"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Non-existent delayed reporting exception"]}, "metadata": {"section": "7", "clause_reference": ["7.1.1(b)", "7.1.1(g)", "7.1.1(h)", "§8.2.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "incident_guidance", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null, "support_citations": ["8.2.1"]}}
{"test_id": "B24-002", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B24", "input": {"question": "Incident response scenario 2: A CII organization experiences a cyber security incident. What CCoP 2.0 Section 8 actions are required for classification and reporting?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "serious", "expected_response": "CCoP 2.0 does not define a Code-level serious/substantial classification scheme or prescribe Form A1/A2 labels or fixed hour-count reporting deadlines in the Code itself. The grounded response is to activate the Cybersecurity Incident Response Plan, follow the incident-reporting structure in the plan so the CIIO complies with the Cybersecurity Act and other applicable laws, contain the affected systems or access path as appropriate, and preserve digital forensic evidence. The CIIO should isolate the affected systems, assess the impact on essential services, and trigger backup, restoration, business continuity or disaster recovery procedures where service delivery is affected. Reference: CCoP 2.0 §7.1.1(b), §7.1.1(g), §7.1.1(h), §8.2.1.", "key_facts": [{"fact": "Serious incident = 2-hour CSA reporting (Form A2)", "source": "CCoP 2.0 Section 8.3", "tier": "critical"}, {"fact": "Substantial incident = 24-hour CSA reporting (Form A1)", "source": "CCoP 2.0 Section 8.3", "tier": "important"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Delayed reporting is acceptable", "Minor incidents don't need reporting"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Non-existent delayed reporting exception"]}, "metadata": {"section": "7", "clause_reference": ["7.1.1(b)", "7.1.1(g)", "7.1.1(h)", "§8.2.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "incident_guidance", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null, "support_citations": ["8.2.1"]}}
{"test_id": "B24-003", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B24", "input": {"question": "Incident response scenario 3: A CII organization experiences a cyber security incident. What CCoP 2.0 Section 8 actions are required for classification and reporting?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "serious", "expected_response": "CCoP 2.0 does not define a Code-level serious/substantial classification scheme or prescribe Form A1/A2 labels or fixed hour-count reporting deadlines in the Code itself. The grounded response is to activate the Cybersecurity Incident Response Plan, follow the incident-reporting structure in the plan so the CIIO complies with the Cybersecurity Act and other applicable laws, contain the affected systems or access path as appropriate, and preserve digital forensic evidence. The CIIO should isolate the affected systems, assess the impact on essential services, and trigger backup, restoration, business continuity or disaster recovery procedures where service delivery is affected. Where essential service delivery is disrupted or at risk, the CIIO should activate the relevant continuity and recovery procedures and restore operations safely. After initial containment, the CIIO should assess impact, determine whether there has been a cybersecurity incident affecting the CII, and perform root-cause analysis where appropriate. Reference: CCoP 2.0 §7.1.1(b), §7.1.1(g), §7.1.1(h), §8.2.1, §7.1.4.", "key_facts": [{"fact": "Serious incident = 2-hour CSA reporting (Form A2)", "source": "CCoP 2.0 Section 8.3", "tier": "critical"}, {"fact": "Substantial incident = 24-hour CSA reporting (Form A1)", "source": "CCoP 2.0 Section 8.3", "tier": "important"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Delayed reporting is acceptable", "Minor incidents don't need reporting"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Non-existent delayed reporting exception"]}, "metadata": {"section": "7", "clause_reference": ["7.1.1(b)", "7.1.1(g)", "7.1.1(i)", "7.1.4", "§8.2.1", "§7.1.4"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "incident_guidance", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null, "support_citations": ["8.2.1"], "clause_reference_original": ["7.1.1(b)", "7.1.1(g)", "7.1.1(i)", "7.1.4"], "clause_reference_corrected_by": "agent-team-2026-04-26", "clause_reference_corrected_verdict": "PARTIAL PASS — original GT is directionally correct but incomplete. The annotator has materially improved coverage by adding 7.1.1(d) and correctly diagnosing the Section 8 misdirection. The GT discrepancy between the two versions (task-prompt vs 30-cases.json) must be resolved. The merged recommended reference set supersedes both GT versions."}}
{"test_id": "B24-004", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B24", "input": {"question": "Incident response scenario 4: A CII organization experiences a cyber security incident. What CCoP 2.0 Section 8 actions are required for classification and reporting?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "serious", "expected_response": "CCoP 2.0 does not define a Code-level serious/substantial classification scheme or prescribe Form A1/A2 labels or fixed hour-count reporting deadlines in the Code itself. The grounded response is to activate the Cybersecurity Incident Response Plan, follow the incident-reporting structure in the plan so the CIIO complies with the Cybersecurity Act and other applicable laws, contain the affected systems or access path as appropriate, and preserve digital forensic evidence. The CIIO should isolate the affected systems, assess the impact on essential services, and trigger backup, restoration, business continuity or disaster recovery procedures where service delivery is affected. Reference: CCoP 2.0 §7.1.1(b), §7.1.1(g), §7.1.1(h), §8.2.1.", "key_facts": [{"fact": "Serious incident = 2-hour CSA reporting (Form A2)", "source": "CCoP 2.0 Section 8.3", "tier": "critical"}, {"fact": "Substantial incident = 24-hour CSA reporting (Form A1)", "source": "CCoP 2.0 Section 8.3", "tier": "important"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Delayed reporting is acceptable", "Minor incidents don't need reporting"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Non-existent delayed reporting exception"]}, "metadata": {"section": "7", "clause_reference": ["7.1.1(d)", "7.1.1(g)", "§8.2.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "incident_guidance", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null, "support_citations": ["8.2.1"]}}
{"test_id": "B24-005", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B24", "input": {"question": "Incident response scenario 5: A CII organization experiences a cyber security incident. What CCoP 2.0 Section 8 actions are required for classification and reporting?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "serious", "expected_response": "CCoP 2.0 does not explicitly prohibit ransom payment but: (1) Classify and report incident first before any payment decision, (2) Activate incident response plan regardless of timing, (3) Preserve forensic evidence, (4) Payment does not exempt reporting requirements, (5) Engage legal/compliance before payment. Rapid payment without proper process may violate Section 8 incident management requirements.", "key_facts": [{"fact": "Serious incident = 2-hour CSA reporting (Form A2)", "source": "CCoP 2.0 Section 8.3", "tier": "critical"}, {"fact": "Substantial incident = 24-hour CSA reporting (Form A1)", "source": "CCoP 2.0 Section 8.3", "tier": "important"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Delayed reporting is acceptable", "Minor incidents don't need reporting"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Non-existent delayed reporting exception"]}, "metadata": {"section": "7", "clause_reference": ["7.1.1(c)", "7.1.1(d)", "7.1.1(e)"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "incident_guidance", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B24-006", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B24", "input": {"question": "Incident response scenario 6: A CII organization experiences a cyber security incident. What CCoP 2.0 Section 8 actions are required for classification and reporting?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"expected_label": "serious", "expected_response": "CCoP 2.0 does not define a Code-level serious/substantial classification scheme or prescribe Form A1/A2 labels or fixed hour-count reporting deadlines in the Code itself. The grounded response is to activate the Cybersecurity Incident Response Plan, follow the incident-reporting structure in the plan so the CIIO complies with the Cybersecurity Act and other applicable laws, contain the affected systems or access path as appropriate, and preserve digital forensic evidence. After initial containment, the CIIO should assess impact, determine whether there has been a cybersecurity incident affecting the CII, and perform root-cause analysis where appropriate. Reference: CCoP 2.0 §7.1.1(b), §7.1.1(g), §7.1.1(h), §7.1.4.", "key_facts": [{"fact": "Serious incident = 2-hour CSA reporting (Form A2)", "source": "CCoP 2.0 Section 8.3", "tier": "critical"}, {"fact": "Substantial incident = 24-hour CSA reporting (Form A1)", "source": "CCoP 2.0 Section 8.3", "tier": "important"}]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Delayed reporting is acceptable", "Minor incidents don't need reporting"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Non-existent delayed reporting exception"]}, "metadata": {"section": "7", "clause_reference": ["7.1.1(b)", "7.1.1(f)", "7.1.1(h)", "§7.1.4"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "incident_guidance", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "negative", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
